# the argument of aquinas-evil-objection.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Aquinas, Summa Theologica I q.2 a.3, Objection 1: the argument from evil, as the objector states it.
# It is not answered here, so it is written as a plain argument rather than as O lines.
atom	god_exists	God exists
atom	infinite_good	there is infinite goodness (one of two contraries, good, is infinite)
atom	infinite_good_2	God's own goodness is unlimited in degree or perfection, as an attribute of one being
atom	evil	there is evil in the world (evil is discoverable)
# S1: if one of two contraries is infinite, the other is altogether destroyed; applied to good and evil.
P1	S1	infinite_good → ¬evil
P2	S2	god_exists → infinite_good_2	kind conceptual
C1	S3	god_exists → ¬evil	from P1 P2
P3	S3	evil	kind empirical
C	S4	¬god_exists	from C1 P3
